    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48173" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">thēsaurizo</span></b> , āre,
			v. n. and <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a.</i> [thesaurus], <i>to gather</i>
			or <i>lay up treasure</i> (late Lat.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Vulg. Bar. 3,
				18</span></i>; Aug. Civ. Dei, 1, 10; <i><span class="en">Salv.
				adv. Avar. 1, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">1, 4
			al.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to treasure up</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">disciplinam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Salv. adv. Avar. 3, 12</span></i>
			: iram, id. Gub. Dei, 5, 9; <i><span class="en">Vulg.
				Jacob. 5, 3</span></i>.</div>
